KW  - Technical debt
KW  - Generative AI
KW  - Large language models
KW  - Technical debt management
AB  - Context:
Generative AI is increasingly applied to Technical Debt Management (TDM), yet their adoption patterns, supported activities, and associated strategies remain fragmented across the literature.
Objective:
This systematic literature review consolidates current research on the integration of Generative AI in TDM, focusing on utilized artifacts, supported activities, architecture models, and role of human involvement.
Method:
We conducted a structured literature review to identify, analyze and synthesize findings from 29 relevant studies, examining how AI is being leveraged to address TD across various dimensions.
Results:
The findings indicate that current approaches primarily support identification and repayment using prompt-based, decoder-only models, while advanced techniques, broader TDM activities, and integrated human collaboration remain limited.
Conclusion:
Current research focuses mainly on artifact-level applications of LLMs, indicating the need for broader TDM coverage, multi-artifact analysis, comparative architectural studies, and stronger human involvement.
ER  - 

